<title>FRANCE: FIRS sees French 97/98 sugar yields at 10 TPH.</title>
<headline>FIRS sees French 97/98 sugar yields at 10 TPH.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Good growing conditions should allow the French 1997/98 beet crop to achieve easily a sugar yield of 10 tonnes per hectare, national sugar intervention board FIRS said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;In France beet conditions up to mid-June allow to expect a yield at least equal to 10 tonnes per hectare,&quot; FIRS said in its June report.</p>
<p>It said the 10 tonnes figure was based on the last five-year average.</p>
<p>In its first forecast for 1997/98 issued in mid-April FIRS had predicted France may produce 4.20 million tonnes of beet sugar compared with 4.226 million in 1996/97.</p>
</text>
